### Fresh database: ids below assume the first user/semester/subject/requirements are 1, 2, ...

### 1. Create a user
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "adi@example.com", "displayName": "Adi" }

### 2. Create a semester (startDate must be a Monday)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users/1/semesters
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "2026/27 Sem 1", "startDate": "2026-10-05", "weeksCount": 14 }

### 3. Create a subject with its required activities
POST http://localhost:8080/api/semesters/1/subjects
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Mobile Systems and Applications",
  "colorHex": "#0288D1",
  "requirements": [
    { "activityType": "LECTURE" },
    { "activityType": "LABORATORY" },
    { "activityType": "CUSTOM", "customTypeName": "Project" }
  ]
}

### 4. Unscheduled activities (the banner)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/semesters/1/requirements/unscheduled

### 5. Schedule the lecture: Monday 08-10, weeks 1-10
POST http://localhost:8080/api/requirements/1/timetable-entries
Content-Type: application/json

{ "dayOfWeek": 1, "startTime": "08:00", "endTime": "10:00", "weekFrom": 1, "weekTo": 10, "room": "A101", "teacher": "Prof. Turing" }

### 6. Laboratory on odd weeks, Monday 10-12
POST http://localhost:8080/api/requirements/2/timetable-entries
Content-Type: application/json

{ "dayOfWeek": 1, "startTime": "10:00", "endTime": "12:00", "weekParity": "ODD", "room": "Lab 302" }

### 7. Overlaps the lecture in weeks 1-10 -> 409 with "conflicts"
POST http://localhost:8080/api/requirements/3/timetable-entries
Content-Type: application/json

{ "dayOfWeek": 1, "startTime": "09:00", "endTime": "11:00" }

### 8. Same request, forced
POST http://localhost:8080/api/requirements/3/timetable-entries?force=true
Content-Type: application/json

{ "dayOfWeek": 1, "startTime": "09:00", "endTime": "11:00" }

### 9. What happens in week 2 (odd lab is hidden)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/semesters/1/timetable?week=2

### 10. Grades and averages
POST http://localhost:8080/api/subjects/1/grades
Content-Type: application/json

{ "score": 9.5, "weight": 1 }

###
POST http://localhost:8080/api/subjects/1/grades
Content-Type: application/json

{ "score": 10, "weight": 1.5 }

###
GET http://localhost:8080/api/subjects/1/grades/summary

###
GET http://localhost:8080/api/semesters/1/gpa
